order_groups.summary:
The CR is used to introduce L1-SINR measurement requirement, which follows the agreement captured in approved WF R4-1915850, R4-2002242 and R4-2005335. Specifially, the following changes are contained:

(1) The changes in the endorsed CR (R4-2005336), including:
Abbrevations for CMR and IMR;
L1-SINR measurement requirement general description;
L1-SINR requirement applicability;
L1-SINR measurement reporting requirement;
L1-SINR measurement requirement for L1-SINR reporting with CSI-RS based CMR and no dedicated IMR configured;
L1-SINR measurement requirement for other two scenarios with dedicated IMR configured;
Measurement restriction for CSI-RS and SSB for L1-SINR;
Schedurling availablity of UE during L1-SINR measurement  (subsection title as placeholder).

(2) Additional changes introduced in this CR: 
L1-SINR measurement requirement for other two scenarios with dedicated IMR configured, in which the following apsects are defined: 
the value of P for sharing factor; 
the scaling factor N under different conditions;
the requriement applicability rules. 
Schedurling availablity of UE during L1-SINR measurement: detailed requirement. 
Capture agreement from 1st round in RAN#95e: “For SSB/CSI-RS-based CMR+IMR L1-SINR measurement: No requirement when CMR or IMR is fully overlapped with MG.”
Clean-up for editor notes.

